---

This package has no runtime dependencies and vendors no third-party code.
Everything it needs — base58, sha256 framing, the ed25519 on-curve test, the
merkle construction — is implemented here against published specifications:

  * ed25519 (RFC 8032) point decompression, in src/curve.mjs, follows the
    procedure in curve25519-dalek's CompressedEdwardsY::decompress.
  * The program-derived-address rule it relies on is Solana's, as documented
    for find_program_address.

Apache-2.0 was chosen over MIT deliberately. This code defines a distribution
mechanism that other people are expected to reimplement in order to check it;
Section 3's express patent grant is the part that matters for that, and a
permissive licence without one would leave a reimplementer worse off than the
original author.
